igned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i} & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(2-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}){x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+(-2-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}){x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the matrix $A-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}I$ is singular, the system above must have a non-zero solution. This means that one equation of the system is a multiple of another. As a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables to be the free variable. For example, from the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{3}(2+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}){x}_{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}(2+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}){x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in C.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=-3,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i} \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{-3}{2+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}}=\\frac{-3(2-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})}{9}=-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\text{i}.$" 13194139535320 true] [17592186343607 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343608 13194139535320 true] [17592186343607 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343609 13194139535320 true] [17592186343607 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343610 13194139535320 true] [17592186343607 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343611 13194139535320 true] [17592186343607 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343612 13194139535320 true] [17592186343607 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535320 true] [17592186343607 1041 "selection" 13194139535320 true] [17592186343607 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343609 13194139535320 true] [17592186343607 1110 #uuid "f5f6cc44-b56b-56a9-84f3-a6bde3a09977" 13194139535320 true] [17592186343608 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\text{i}" 13194139535320 true] [17592186343608 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535320 true] [17592186343608 1111 #uuid "0192428f-d96f-526b-a0c5-e2b086a252b1" 13194139535320 true] [175921